</ptxt>
<step1>
<ptxt>Vehicle Battery Power Saving Function</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>In the smart entry &amp; start system (smart entry), a request signal is periodically transmitted every 0.25 seconds during standby to form the detection area, so the battery may discharge if the vehicle is left for a long time. To prevent battery discharge, the following control is set.</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>If there is no response from the electrical key transmitter for 5 days or more, the periodic request signal transmission interval is extended to 0.75 seconds.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>If there is no response from the electrical key transmitter for 14 days or more, and 10 minutes or more have elapsed with the electrical key transmitter in the detection area (including inside the vehicle), smart entry &amp; start system control is stopped.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>The smart entry function is restored when any of the following operations is performed.</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>When locking/unlocking by wireless operation.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>When locking by pressing the lock switch of the door outside handle assembly RH or LH.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>When locking/unlocking by inserting the mechanical key into the driver side door key cylinder.</ptxt>
</step3>
</step2>
</step1>
